-- title:
--   Tame monodromy bound for ℓ^k-torsion of J_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a positive integer with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ contain the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral-form ratios for $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and fix a model datum $\mathfrak{X}$ of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, level data $\Lambda$ and an object $O$ of `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM A hA Λ`, together with the assumption that the designation built from $O.G$, $O.g$ and the unit section represents the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles on $\mathfrak{X}$ that are fibrewise algebraically trivial (the condition `algEquivZeroCut`, rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\mathrm{inf}}$). Let $\ell \neq p$ be a prime, $k \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $\gamma$ lie in the inertia subgroup $I_A =$ `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` of $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ be such that every $\tau \in I_A$ can be written $\gamma^{j} x^{\ell^k} w^{\ell^k}$ with $j \in \mathbb{N}$ and $x, w \in I_A$. Write $J = J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones) and $J[\ell^k]$ for its $\ell^k$-torsion. Assume that $\sigma \cdot x - x \in O.\mathrm{toricPts}(\ell^k)$, the subgroup generated by the toric points $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,\ell^k$, for all $\sigma \in I_A$ and all $x \in J[\ell^k]$. Then $$\#J[\ell^k] \le \#\{\gamma \cdot x - x : x \in J[\ell^k]\} \cdot \#\{x \in J[\ell^k] : \sigma \cdot x = x \text{ for all } \sigma \in I_A\}.$$
--
--   This is the monodromy count underlying the analysis of $J_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level: the toric displacement hypothesis forces tame inertia to act through a single generator $\gamma$ on the $\ell^k$-torsion, so that the torsion is bounded by the displacement image times the inertia invariants. It is used in the construction of inertia displacements with prescribed toric behaviour, [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner).
